===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er}}

# Having a [[slippery]] surface; having a surface covered with [[grease]].
#: {{ux|en|a '''greasy''' mineral}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Antony and Cleopatra|V|2|text={{...}} mechanic slaves<br>With '''greasy''' aprons, rules, and hammers, shall<br>Uplift us to the view {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1961|author={{w|V. S. Naipaul}}|title={{w|A House for Mr Biswas}}|location=London|publisher=André Deutsch|section=Part One, Chapter 2, p. 54|url=https://archive.org/details/in.ernet.dli.2015.149342
|passage=it was in the garage that Alec worked, {{...}} doing mysterious '''greasy''' things. Grease blackened his hairy legs; grease had turned his white canvas shoes black; grease blackened his hands even beyond the wrist; grease made his short working trousers black and stiff. Yet he had the gift, which Mr Biswas admired, of being able to hold a cigarette between '''greasy''' fingers and '''greasy''' lips without staining it.}}
# Containing a lot of [[grease]] or fat.
#* {{circa|1795}}, Margaret Taylor, ''Mrs. Taylor’s Family Companion: or The Whole Art of Cookery Display’d'', London: W. Lane, “To fry flat Fish,” p. 37,<sup>[http://name.umdl.umich.edu/004826650.0001.000]</sup>
#*: Before you dish them up, lay them upon a drainer before the fire sloping, for two or three minutes, which will prevent their eating '''greasy'''.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2010|author=Gavin Hoffen|title=Dandelion|page=3|passage=With a skin full of alcohol and a probable overwhelming desire for a '''greasy''' kebab, I had evidently got myself into such a state that I was unable to locate the correct door to the fast food shop.}}
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|date=May 3, 2012
|author=Felicity Cloake
|title=How to cook perfect garlic bread
|work=the Guardian
|url=http://www.guardian.co.uk/lifeandstyle/wordofmouth/2012/may/03/how-to-cook-perfect-garlic-bread?INTCMP=SRCH
|page=
|passage=Nigel and Richard Bertinet go for butter. Jamie and Nigella both opt for olive oil, and Garten uses a mixture, spreading the bread generously with butter, then topping it with garlic and herbs in olive oil. Oil, to my taste, simply makes the bread seem '''greasy''': it's great for dipping, but it doesn't seem to soak into the bread in the same way as butter – I've probably just got hopelessly rich Anglo-Saxon tastes, but for me, it's butter all the way.}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} [[shady]], [[sketchy]], [[dodgy]], [[detestable]], [[unethical]].
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|year=2004
|month=April 25
|title=Trailer Park Boys episode "Rub N Tiz'zug"
|url=http://en.wikiquote.org/wiki/Trailer_Park_Boys
|passage=''Julian:'' We're gonna fill the trailers up with furniture all right, boys, but we're gonna rent them out by the hour.<br/> ''Bubbles:'' Aw, that's '''greasy'''.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[fat]], [[bulky]]
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Merry Wives|II|1|text=Let’s consult together against this '''greasy''' knight.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[gross]]; [[indelicate]]; [[indecent]]
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1601|author={{w|John Marston (poet)|John Marston}}|title={{w|Jack Drum's Entertainment|Jack Drum’s Entertainment}}|location=London|publisher=Richard Olive|section=Act I|url=http://name.umdl.umich.edu/A20867.0001.001
|passage=Now I am perfect hate, I [[love|lou’d]] but three things in the world, Philosophy, Thrift, and my self. Thou hast made me hate Philosophy. A [[usurer|Vsurers]] '''greasie''' [[codpiece|Codpeece]] made me loath Thrift: but if all the Brewers [[jade|Iades]] in the town can drug me from [[love|loue]] of my selfe, they shall doo more then e’re the seuen wise men of ''Greece'' could {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|of a horse}} Afflicted with the disease called [[grease]].

